{"node_id":"LVMC_11_12_070_B","law_refs":["LVMC-11-12-070-B"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"Said driver","role":"condition"},{"id":"s2","text":"having so yielded","role":"condition"},{"id":"s3","text":"may proceed","role":"condition"},{"id":"s4","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"s5","text":"the drivers of all other vehicles","role":"subject"},{"id":"s6","text":"approaching the intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"s7","text":"on the through highway","role":"condition"},{"id":"s8","text":"shall yield","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s9","text":"right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"s10","text":"to the vehicle about to enter or cross the through highway","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"s5","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicles' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate: the atom's literal argument is an aggregate id'. Its exclusion 'a relational role such as who drives or controls a vehicle — never membership' does not apply: 'the drivers of' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency reading), and the aggregate only states the class. 'all other' = every vehicle other than the one about to enter: the subject is never the same road user as o."},{"span":"s6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.lane_enters: 'a road user's approach to an intersection is a carrier it occupies (rel.occupies) whose entrance end is that intersection ... approaches through it whatever its motion'. The carrier c is quantified over st.travel_region (the abstract union of the carrier kinds lane_enters admits) and the intersection j over st.intersection ('the region where two roadways meet'). Not a stand-in for the subject's presence in the intersection or for dev.governs: the relation read is entry topology, as its contract states."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","dev.traffic_signal","dev.governs","st.lane_enters","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"DEF-NRS-484A-275: a through highway is one 'at the entrances to which vehicular traffic from intersecting highways is required by law to yield right-of-way to vehicles on such through highway in obedience to either an authorized stop sign or a yield sign, or other official traffic-control device'. Read on the devices: the subject's approach carrier c is governed (dev.governs: 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls') by no stop sign ('regulatory sign requiring a full halt'), yield sign ('regulatory sign requiring yielding without a mandatory halt') or traffic signal showing flashing_red, while the entering vehicle's carrier c2 into the same j is governed by one of them. dev.governs 'Not a stand-in for: a position' does not apply: governance, not a halting place, is read."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.contact"],"derived":[],"justification":"To yield is to grant the other precedence: the subject does not proceed in conflict with it. kin.speed 'magnitude of velocity' tells a subject still proceeding from one that has given way; rel.contact 'the bodies of two road users ... touch or overlap (a collision)' marks precedence taken outright. rel.contact's exclusion 'a near miss' is respected: the near-conflict is bounded by the operationalization of s9, not by contact."},{"span":"s10","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","rel.occupies","st.intersection","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (ru.aggregate, as on s5). 'about to enter or cross the through highway' is an imminent movement, read by the movement it leads to: o, coming from carrier c2 with st.lane_enters(c2, j), occupies j (rel.occupies 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region (... intersection ...)') now or at an observation within p.conflict_horizon ahead; j is the intersection of the through highway the subject approaches (st.intersection)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"s9","standard":"right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210 'approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other'","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","kin.speed"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: a danger of a crash exists where, under constant velocities, the centres of the two road users come within a centre clearance comparable to their half-extents inside a time-to-collision horizon; a road user whose speed is at or below the source's speed resolution has granted precedence","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[{"span":"s1","rule":"LVMC_11_12_070_A","map":{"subject":"o"},"as":"condition"},{"span":"s2","rule":"LVMC_11_12_070_A","map":{"subject":"o"},"as":"compliance"}],"residues":[{"span":"s3","why":"a permission granted to the entering driver; it imposes no condition on the through-highway drivers beyond the entering vehicle's movement, which s10 carries, so the duty is the same whether or not the permission is read","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), occupies a carrier c (st.travel_region) with st.lane_enters(c, j) for an intersection j (st.intersection), and c is governed (dev.governs) by no stop sign, no yield sign and no traffic signal showing flashing_red; and some road user o, not the subject, is a vehicle (same aggregate) that came from a carrier c2 with st.lane_enters(c2, j) governed by a stop sign, a yield sign or a traffic signal showing flashing_red, and either occupies j (having occupied c2 or j at every observation since it last occupied c2) or occupies c2 and occupies j at some observation within p.conflict_horizon ahead; and LVMC_11_12_070_A applies to o (o mapped to its subject) and o complies with it.","obligation":"For every road user o selected as in the applicability (re-bound with the whole selection: a vehicle other than the subject, from a carrier c2 entering the same j governed by a stop sign, yield sign or flashing-red signal, entering j within p.conflict_horizon or already in j having come from c2, LVMC_11_12_070_A applying to it and complied with): it is not the case that the subject's kin.speed exceeds p.halt_speed_tolerance while prim.closest_approach_within(subject, o; p.conflict_horizon) holds with prim.closest_approach_distance(subject, o; p.conflict_horizon) below p.conflict_centre_clearance; and rel.contact(subject, o) does not hold.","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s5","why":"'drivers' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: the duty binds the vehicle approaching on the through highway, whoever or whatever controls it","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"s7","why":"the legal designation 'through highway' is read through the devices on the road that display it: a stop sign, a yield sign or a flashing-red signal governing the entering approach and none governing the subject's approach; 'other official traffic-control device' is read as the flashing-red signal, the remaining device that requires traffic from the intersecting highway to halt and yield","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"s10","why":"'about to enter or cross' is an imminent movement, read by the entry into the intersection it leads to (within p.conflict_horizon ahead) or by the vehicle already crossing","kind":"observable_reading","category":"intention"},{"span":"s9","why":"precedence is read as the subject not proceeding (speed above the halt tolerance) while a constant-velocity closest approach to the entering vehicle falls below the centre clearance within the horizon, and never touching it; how the subject gives way (slowing or halting) is not modelled","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Subject vehicle on a lane entering j with no device; o halted at the stop sign on the cross approach, complied with LVMC_11_12_070_A, then moves into j; the subject keeps its speed and the constant-velocity closest approach of centres is below p.conflict_centre_clearance within p.conflict_horizon."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same scene; the subject brakes to a halt short of j while o crosses; while the closest approach is below the clearance the subject's speed is at or below p.halt_speed_tolerance, and no contact occurs."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject approaches j on the through approach, but no vehicle is on or entering from a stop-sign or yield-sign approach of j."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"As forbid, but the source does not observe which carriers the stop sign governs, so whether o's approach is an entrance to a through highway is unknown.","masked":["dev.governs"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"All-way stop: the subject's own carrier is governed by a stop sign, so it is not on a through highway."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique: a closest approach later than this is not a present danger of a crash","source":"Hayward (1972) time-to-collision; Swedish Traffic Conflict Technique (Hydén 1987)"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies of a passenger car and another road user are taken to collide or nearly collide: about a car's half-length plus half a body width","source":"passenger-car dimensions (AASHTO design vehicle P: 5.8 m by 2.1 m)"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed noise floor of vehicle odometry and tracked-object estimates"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_16_030","law_refs":["LVMC-11-16-030"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"c1","text":"The prima facie speed limit shall be fifteen miles per hour","role":"obligation"},{"id":"c2","text":"when traversing a grade crossing","role":"trigger"},{"id":"c3","text":"of a steam, electric or any other motor railway","role":"condition"},{"id":"c4","text":"if during the last one hundred feet of the approach to such crossing","role":"condition"},{"id":"c5","text":"the driver","role":"subject"},{"id":"c6","text":"does not have a clear and unobstructed view of such crossing and of any traffic on such railway for a distance of four hundred feet in both directions along such railway","role":"condition"},{"id":"c7","text":"This Section shall not apply in the case of any railway grade crossing where a human flagman is on duty","role":"exception"},{"id":"c8","text":"or clearly visible electrical or mechanical railway crossing signal device is installed but does not then indicate the immediate approach of a railway train or car","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"c1","atoms":["kin.speed"],"derived":[],"justification":"kin.speed 'magnitude of velocity' in m/s is the speed the limit bounds; its exclusion of acceleration does not apply."},{"span":"c2","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.railway_crossing"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.railway_crossing 'level crossing of a railway with the roadway' is the grade crossing; traversing it is the subject's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region')."},{"span":"c4","atoms":["kin.path_length","rel.occupies","st.railway_crossing"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the last one hundred feet of the approach' is a window measured in distance travelled (a .path window), which reads kin.path_length 'distance travelled along the body's path'; the window ends at the observation at which the subject's occupancy of the crossing rose (rel.occupies, st.railway_crossing)."},{"span":"c5","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the driver' (DEF-NRS-484A-080: 'every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle') is read through the controlled motion of the vehicle the driver drives; the vehicle is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, and ru.aggregate's exclusion of 'who drives or controls a vehicle' is respected: the role is read through motion, the aggregate gives the class."},{"span":"c6","atoms":["st.sight_along_way","st.sight_distance","rel.visible","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","ru.rail_vehicle","st.railway_crossing"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only (gap): st.sight_along_way is 'the distance along a way ... within which another vehicle on that way could be seen', a way being a public way (st.highway), not a railway; st.sight_distance is 'the distance along the road'; rel.visible concerns an actual road user ('Not a stand-in for ... the sight distance of a place'). 'traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic and the trains are ru.rail_vehicle, but the clause needs the sight along the railway whether or not a train is there. Literal four hundred feet."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"c3","why":"every railway the ontology's st.railway_crossing covers is one of steam, electric or any other motor railway; the words list kinds without excluding any, so the duty is the same whether or not they are read","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle, occupies a railway crossing x (st.railway_crossing); at some observation within the last one hundred feet of path (kin.path_length, a .path window) before the observation at which its occupancy of x rose, the sight along the railway from the subject, in both directions, fell short of four hundred feet or the crossing was not in view (no atom: gap); and neither exception holds: no flagger or railroad flagger (dev.human_direction) governs a carrier the subject occupies at x, and no railway signal or gate (dev.railway_signal_or_gate) governing such a carrier shows lights dark with gate up or none and bell silent.","obligation":"At every observation at which the subject occupies x, its kin.speed is at most fifteen miles per hour.","params":[],"narrowings":[{"span":"c1","why":"a prima facie limit is read as a maximum: a speed above it is reported violated; the rebuttal a court may admit is not modelled","kind":"reading"},{"span":"c5","why":"'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"c7","why":"'on duty' is read through the flagger's presence directing traffic at the crossing","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"c8","why":"'clearly visible ... installed' is read through the device's presence governing the subject's carrier at the crossing","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Subject approaches an unsignalled crossing with buildings blocking the view along the railway in the last 100 ft and traverses it above fifteen mph."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same, traversing at or below fifteen mph."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"Crossing equipped with a railway signal whose lights are dark and gate up while the subject traverses it."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The source does not observe sight along the way; the view condition is unknown.","masked":["st.sight_along_way"]}],"literals":[{"span":"c1","text":"fifteen miles per hour","value":15,"unit":"mph"},{"span":"c4","text":"one hundred feet","value":100,"unit":"ft"},{"span":"c6","text":"four hundred feet","value":400,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[],"gaps":[{"span":"c6","kind":"atom","proposal":"`st.sight_along_railway` | the distance along a railway, in each direction from its crossing with the roadway, within which a rail vehicle on that railway could be seen from a road user's eye at the observation, at the height convention the source declares; the smaller of the two directions; m **Not a stand-in for:** the sight along a public way (`st.sight_along_way`), the sight distance of a place on the road (`st.sight_distance`), or whether an actual rail vehicle is seen (`rel.visible`) | general","nearest":"st.sight_along_way (excluded: 'along a way ... another vehicle on that way' — a public way, not a railway); st.sight_distance ('the distance along the road'); rel.visible ('Not a stand-in for: ... the sight distance of a place'). The distinction decided: where the reduced limit applies to a road user traversing a grade crossing."}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_16_040","law_refs":["LVMC-11-16-040"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"d1","text":"The prima facie speed limit shall be fifteen miles per hour","role":"obligation"},{"id":"d2","text":"when traversing any intersection","role":"trigger"},{"id":"d3","text":"or street or highway","role":"condition"},{"id":"d4","text":"if during the last one hundred feet of his approach to such intersection","role":"condition"},{"id":"d5","text":"the driver","role":"subject"},{"id":"d6","text":"does not have a clear and unobstructed view of such intersection","role":"condition"},{"id":"d7","text":"and of any traffic upon all of the streets or highways entering such intersection","role":"condition"},{"id":"d8","text":"for a distance of one hundred feet along all such streets or highways","role":"condition"},{"id":"d9","text":"except on a through street or highway","role":"exception"},{"id":"d10","text":"or at a traffic-controlled intersection","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"d1","atoms":["kin.speed"],"derived":[],"justification":"kin.speed 'magnitude of velocity' in m/s is the speed the limit bounds; its exclusion of acceleration does not apply."},{"span":"d2","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.intersection 'the region where two roadways meet' (DEF-NRS-484A-105 'the area embraced within the prolongation or connection of the lateral curb lines'); traversing it is the subject's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies). Its exclusion 'a crosswalk or a stop line' does not apply: the region itself is read."},{"span":"d4","atoms":["kin.path_length","rel.occupies","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the last one hundred feet of his approach' is a .path window, reading kin.path_length 'distance travelled along the body's path', ending at the observation at which the subject's occupancy of j (rel.occupies, st.intersection) rose; the window is the subject's own path before that entry."},{"span":"d5","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'the driver' (DEF-NRS-484A-080 'every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle') is read through the controlled motion of the vehicle, the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; ru.aggregate's exclusion of 'who drives or controls a vehicle' is respected: the role is read through motion, the aggregate gives the class."},{"span":"d6","atoms":["st.sight_distance","st.region_geometry","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.sight_distance 'the distance along the road within which a vehicle at a point and another vehicle on the road could see each other ... whether or not any road user is there': the view of the intersection is clear where the sight distance at the subject's point is at least the ground distance from its body to j (st.region_geometry 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it'). Its exclusions (rel.visible, env.visibility) do not apply: the view of a place, not of an actual road user, is read."},{"span":"d7","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.visible","rel.occupies","st.on_way","st.highway","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"'traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic. The streets or highways entering j are the ways w (st.highway 'the entire public way between its boundary lines') with st.on_way(j, w) ('an intersection lies on every way that meets there'). A view of any traffic upon them is, for every traffic member o occupying w (rel.occupies) whose ground distance to j (st.region_geometry) is within one hundred feet, rel.visible(subject, o) 'an unobstructed line of sight from a's reference point to b's body'; its exclusion of the sight distance of a place does not apply since d8 carries that."},{"span":"d8","atoms":["st.sight_along_way","st.on_way","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.sight_along_way 'the distance along a way, in each direction from the point of that way nearest a road user, within which another vehicle on that way could be seen from the road user's eye ...; the smaller of the two directions' is read for every way w with st.on_way(j, w) and compared with the literal one hundred feet; its exclusions (st.sight_distance, rel.visible) do not apply: the sight along each entering way is what the words measure."},{"span":"d9","atoms":["dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","dev.traffic_signal","dev.governs","st.lane_enters","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"DEF-NRS-484A-275 'at the entrances to which vehicular traffic from intersecting highways is required by law to yield right-of-way to vehicles on such through highway in obedience to either an authorized stop sign or a yield sign, or other official traffic-control device': the subject's approach carrier c (the carrier it occupied, st.lane_enters(c, j), at the last observation before its entry into j) is governed (dev.governs) by no stop sign, yield sign or flashing-red traffic signal, while another carrier entering j is governed by one of them. Same reading as LVMC_11_12_070_B s7. dev.governs 'Not a stand-in for: a position' does not apply."},{"span":"d10","atoms":["dev.traffic_signal","dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","dev.governs","st.lane_enters","st.travel_region","st.intersection"],"derived":[],"justification":"A traffic-controlled intersection is one whose traffic a control device controls: a traffic signal ('a signal head') in a state other than dark, a stop sign or a yield sign governs (dev.governs: 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection') j itself or a carrier c with st.lane_enters(c, j). dev.governs 'no closure to the lanes that enter it' is respected by reading both the junction and the entering carriers explicitly."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"d3","why":"every intersection is, by DEF-NRS-484A-105, a junction of highways and streets; the words add no region beyond the intersection whose approach the condition measures, so the duty is the same whether or not they are read","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle, occupies an intersection j (st.intersection); and at some observation of the .path window of one hundred feet (kin.path_length) behind the observation at which its occupancy of j rose, the view was not clear: the subject's st.sight_distance was below its ground distance to j, or for some way w with st.on_way(j, w) its st.sight_along_way(w) was below one hundred feet, or some traffic member o (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic) occupying such a w within one hundred feet of j (st.region_geometry distance) was not rel.visible from the subject; and not (d9) the subject's approach carrier at its entry into j was governed by no stop sign, yield sign or flashing-red signal while another carrier entering j was governed by one; and not (d10) a traffic signal in a state other than dark, a stop sign or a yield sign governs j or a carrier entering j.","obligation":"At every observation at which the subject occupies j, its kin.speed is at most fifteen miles per hour.","params":[],"narrowings":[{"span":"d1","why":"a prima facie limit is read as a maximum: a speed above it is reported violated; the rebuttal a court may admit is not modelled","kind":"reading"},{"span":"d5","why":"'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"d9","why":"the legal designation 'through street or highway' is read through the devices on the road that display it (stop sign, yield sign, flashing-red signal governing the entering approaches)","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Uncontrolled intersection, hedges limit sight along the cross street to 20 m during the last 100 ft of the subject's approach; it traverses j above fifteen mph."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same, traversing j at or below fifteen mph."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"Same restricted view, but a traffic signal (circular_green) governs the subject's approach lane."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Uncontrolled intersection; the source does not supply sight along the ways, and the subject traverses above fifteen mph.","masked":["st.sight_along_way"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Clear view everywhere (sight distance and sight along every way beyond the bounds), no other road user in the scene; the subject traverses at any speed: the condition does not hold for lack of view, so with no traffic present the clear view is decided and the reduced limit does not apply — expected not engaged is reported only where the view is clear; here the view is restricted by a wall on one way and no road user is present, and the subject traverses at or below fifteen mph."}],"literals":[{"span":"d1","text":"fifteen miles per hour","value":15,"unit":"mph"},{"span":"d4","text":"one hundred feet","value":100,"unit":"ft"},{"span":"d8","text":"one hundred feet","value":100,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_16_060","law_refs":["LVMC-11-16-060"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"f1","text":"The prima facie speed limit is twenty-five miles per hour","role":"obligation"},{"id":"f2","text":"on all streets and highways","role":"condition"},{"id":"f3","text":"unless a different speed limit is posted as set forth in this Title","role":"exception"}],"elements":[{"span":"f1","atoms":["kin.speed"],"derived":[],"justification":"kin.speed 'magnitude of velocity' in m/s is the speed the limit bounds; its exclusion of acceleration does not apply. A speed limit binds the vehicle travelling there: the subject is a vehicle (DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle)."},{"span":"f2","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.highway 'the entire public way between its boundary lines'; streets (DEF-NRS-484A-265, highways inside a city) and highways together are every highway, so the city limit, a legal region class, is not needed. The subject is on one where its footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies). st.highway 'Not a stand-in for: the roadway' does not apply: the words name the whole way."},{"span":"f3","atoms":["dev.speed_limit_sign","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.speed_limit_sign 'sign stating a maximum or minimum speed, with value and unit; kind ∈ {maximum, minimum, structure_maximum, zone}': a posted limit is a sign of kind maximum, structure_maximum or zone governing (dev.governs 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls') a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies. 'posted as set forth in this Title' is the legal status of the posting, read through the sign's presence. A minimum is no different speed limit in the sense of a maximum replacing the prima facie one."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), occupies a highway region w (st.highway); and no speed limit sign of kind maximum, structure_maximum or zone governs (dev.governs) a travel region (st.travel_region) the subject occupies.","obligation":"The subject's kin.speed is at most twenty-five miles per hour.","params":[],"narrowings":[{"span":"f1","why":"a prima facie limit is read as a maximum: a speed above it is reported violated; the rebuttal a court may admit is not modelled","kind":"reading"},{"span":"f3","why":"'posted as set forth in this Title' is read through the presence of the posted speed limit sign governing the subject's travel region","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Subject on a street lane governed by no speed limit sign travels above twenty-five mph."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same, at or below twenty-five mph."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject's lane is governed by a maximum speed limit sign (45 mph posting)."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"A speed limit sign is present but the source does not observe what it governs; subject above twenty-five mph.","masked":["dev.governs"]}],"literals":[{"span":"f1","text":"twenty-five miles per hour","value":25,"unit":"mph"}],"param_proposals":[],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_16_090_A_o1","law_refs":["LVMC-11-16-090-A"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"g1","text":"No person shall engage in","role":"obligation"},{"id":"g2","text":"any motor vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"g3","text":"speed contest or exhibition of power or speed","role":"standard"},{"id":"g4","text":"on a highway","role":"condition"},{"id":"g5","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g6","text":"no person shall aid or abet in","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g7","text":"any such motor vehicle","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g8","text":"speed contest or exhibition","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g9","text":"upon any highway","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"g1","atoms":["kin.accel_longitudinal","kin.speed"],"derived":[],"justification":"Engaging is read through the subject vehicle's own conduct: kin.accel_longitudinal 'acceleration along heading, signed' ('Not a stand-in for: speed' respected: both are read separately) and kin.speed 'magnitude of velocity'. The person who engages is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency)."},{"span":"g2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'motor vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle; ru.aggregate: 'membership of a legal aggregate'. The contest is one in a motor vehicle, so the subject is a member; the other party of a contest is a member too."},{"span":"g4","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.highway 'the entire public way between its boundary lines'; the subject is on it where its footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies). 'Not a stand-in for: the roadway' does not apply: the words name the highway."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"g3","standard":"speed contest or exhibition of power or speed","concepts":["kin.accel_longitudinal","kin.speed","rel.same_direction","rel.longitudinal_overlap","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"params":["p.exhibition_accel_min","p.exhibition_speed_min","p.contest_accel_min","p.contest_window","p.contest_same_direction_cos"],"convention":"naturalistic-driving harsh-event thresholds: an exhibition of power is a longitudinal acceleration above a harsh-acceleration threshold, an exhibition of speed a speed above a bound far beyond any posted limit, and a contest two motor vehicles side by side in the same direction both accelerating above a lower threshold throughout a window","surrogate":true}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a motor vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle), occupies a highway region (st.highway, rel.occupies).","obligation":"Not any of: (a) the subject's kin.accel_longitudinal is at least p.exhibition_accel_min; (b) its kin.speed is at least p.exhibition_speed_min; (c) at every observation of the time window p.contest_window behind, some other road user o that is a motor vehicle (same aggregate) has rel.same_direction(subject, o; p.contest_same_direction_cos), positive rel.longitudinal_overlap with the subject, and both the subject's and o's kin.accel_longitudinal are at least p.contest_accel_min (o bound inside the window, one road user throughout).","params":["p.exhibition_accel_min","p.exhibition_speed_min","p.contest_accel_min","p.contest_window","p.contest_same_direction_cos"],"narrowings":[{"span":"g1","why":"'person ... engage' is read through the controlled motion of the motor vehicle the person drives","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"g3","why":"a contest or exhibition is a purpose shown in conduct; it is read only through acceleration, speed and side-by-side acceleration with another motor vehicle; burnouts, wheel spin and sliding manoeuvres are not read","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"Two motor vehicles side by side in the same direction on a highway both accelerating above p.contest_accel_min for the whole p.contest_window."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject accelerates moderately from a light, below every bound, alone in its direction."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject is in a private parking lot that is no highway region."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Accelerations are not observed and the subject's speed is below the speed bound.","masked":["kin.accel_longitudinal"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"No other road user in the scene; the subject alone accelerates above p.exhibition_accel_min (exhibition of power)."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.exhibition_accel_min","unit":"m/s²","value":4.0,"convention":"harsh-acceleration threshold: a longitudinal acceleration of about 0.4 g, beyond ordinary driving","source":"naturalistic driving studies' harsh-event thresholds (e.g. SHRP2, 100-Car study)"},{"name":"p.exhibition_speed_min","unit":"m/s","value":44.7,"convention":"a speed of about 100 mph, beyond any posted limit in the jurisdiction","source":"highest posted limits in Nevada (80 mph) plus a margin"},{"name":"p.contest_accel_min","unit":"m/s²","value":2.5,"convention":"a sustained acceleration well above ordinary launches (about 0.25 g) held by both vehicles","source":"naturalistic driving acceleration distributions"},{"name":"p.contest_window","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"duration a side-by-side hard acceleration must last to be a contest rather than a merge","source":"drag-race launch durations"},{"name":"p.contest_same_direction_cos","unit":"1","value":0.95,"convention":"cosine of the largest heading difference (about 18 degrees) for travel in the same direction","source":"lane-level heading alignment tolerance"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_16_090_A_o2","law_refs":["LVMC-11-16-090-A"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.subject"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"g1","text":"No person shall engage in","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g2","text":"any motor vehicle","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g3","text":"speed contest or exhibition of power or speed","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g4","text":"on a highway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"g5","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"g6","text":"no person shall aid or abet in","role":"obligation"},{"id":"g7","text":"any such motor vehicle","role":"condition"},{"id":"g8","text":"speed contest or exhibition","role":"standard"},{"id":"g9","text":"upon any highway","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"g6","atoms":["rel.centre_distance","dev.human_direction"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only (gap): rel.centre_distance is a distance ('Not a stand-in for ... an order of arrival'), proximity to a contest is not aiding it; dev.human_direction is 'a person directing traffic' with roles police_officer, flagger, school_crossing_guard, railroad_flagger, none of which is a person starting or flagging a race. No atom records assisting another's contest."},{"span":"g7","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'motor vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-130::motor_vehicle; the other party b whose contest is aided is a member."},{"span":"g9","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.highway 'the entire public way between its boundary lines'; the contest b engages in is on it (rel.occupies)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"g8","standard":"speed contest or exhibition (the one LVMC_11_16_090_A_o1 forbids, of the other party b)","concepts":["kin.accel_longitudinal","kin.speed","rel.same_direction","rel.longitudinal_overlap"],"params":["p.exhibition_accel_min","p.exhibition_speed_min","p.contest_accel_min","p.contest_window","p.contest_same_direction_cos"],"convention":"as LVMC_11_16_090_A_o1: naturalistic-driving harsh-event thresholds applied to the other party","surrogate":true}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.subject"]}],"applicability":"Some road user b other than the subject, a motor vehicle on a highway, engages at the observation in a speed contest or exhibition as LVMC_11_16_090_A_o1's operationalization reads it.","obligation":"The subject does not assist b's contest or exhibition (no atom: gap).","params":["p.exhibition_accel_min","p.exhibition_speed_min","p.contest_accel_min","p.contest_window","p.contest_same_direction_cos"],"narrowings":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A person on the roadway flags the start of two motor vehicles racing side by side."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A pedestrian on the sidewalk walks past while two vehicles race; it does nothing for them."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"No motor vehicle in the scene exceeds any contest or exhibition bound."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"Accelerations are not observed, so whether a contest is under way is unknown.","masked":["kin.accel_longitudinal"]}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[],"gaps":[{"span":"g6","kind":"atom","proposal":"`rel.contest_assistance` | relation: road user a assists road user b's speed contest or exhibition on the road — starting or flagging it, blocking or holding traffic or a way for it, or escorting it — as the source records the act **Not a stand-in for:** proximity to, travel beside or watching the contest | general","nearest":"rel.centre_distance ('Not a stand-in for: a clearance between bodies or an order of arrival' — proximity is no assistance); dev.human_direction (roles police_officer, flagger, school_crossing_guard, railroad_flagger: directing traffic, not a race start). The distinction decided: which road users the prohibition concerns — those who take part in another's contest without driving in it."}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_18_020","law_refs":["LVMC-11-18-020"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"k1","text":"The City Traffic Engineer is authorized to mark and maintain with yellow paint or road buttons crosswalks approximately twelve feet in width at intersections in the vicinity of schools where in the opinion of the City Traffic Engineer crossing the roadway by schoolchildren is unsafe.","role":"definitional"},{"id":"k2","text":"The City Traffic Engineer, if necessary, is further authorized to mark and maintain with a distinguishing color or road buttons upon the pavement or by signs erected along the curb in a conspicuous manner, the words \"School-Xing,\" not less than one hundred feet in advance of each crosswalk established","role":"definitional"},{"id":"k3","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"k4","text":"it shall be unlawful for the operator of any vehicle to drive into a crosswalk","role":"obligation"},{"id":"k5","text":"where there is displayed a sign with the words \"School-Xing,\"","role":"condition"},{"id":"k6","text":"when there is in the crosswalk","role":"condition"},{"id":"k7","text":"upon the side of the roadway on which said vehicle is coming","role":"condition"},{"id":"k8","text":"any person","role":"condition"},{"id":"k9","text":"attempting to cross the street","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"k4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'the operator of' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency), never as membership. 'drive into a crosswalk' is the observation at which the subject's footprint begins to overlap (rel.occupies rises) a crosswalk cw (st.crosswalk 'marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection'); 'Not a stand-in for' clauses of rel.occupies are none, and st.sidewalk's exclusion of crosswalks is not engaged."},{"span":"k5","atoms":["dev.zone_sign","dev.governs","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","rel.occupies","st.travel_region","st.intersection","st.crosswalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.zone_sign 'a sign that begins or ends a signed zone along the road; kind ∈ {school, school_crossing, ...}': the 'School-Xing' sign is kind school_crossing. It is the sign of that crosswalk: it governs (dev.governs 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls') the carrier c the subject occupies (rel.occupies), whose entrance into intersection j (st.lane_enters) the crosswalk marks (st.entrance_of 'the carrier whose entrance into an intersection a stop line or a crosswalk marks'). dev.zone_sign's exclusion 'whether the condition holds now' is respected: no condition of the legend is read; dev.governs 'Not a stand-in for: a position' does not apply."},{"span":"k6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.crosswalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"The person o is in the crosswalk cw the subject drives into: rel.occupies(o, cw) 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region (... crosswalk ...)'."},{"span":"k7","atoms":["st.centre_line","prim.region_lateral_offset","rel.bearing","st.on_way","st.highway","st.one_way_roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"The side of the roadway the subject comes on is its side of the centre line (st.centre_line 'the marking, or the geometric centre, dividing the two directions of a two-way roadway') of the way w the crosswalk lies on (st.on_way(cw, w), st.on_way(cl, w), st.highway). With L = prim.region_lateral_offset(subject, cl) ('the signed lateral offset ... of a structure region from a road user', left positive) and y the lateral component of rel.bearing(subject, o) ('direction of b from a in a's frame'), o is on the subject's side where L > 0 and y < L, or L < 0 and y > L. Where the subject occupies a one-way roadway (st.one_way_roadway 'roadway on which traffic is restricted to one direction'), the whole crosswalk is its side."},{"span":"k8","atoms":["ru.pedestrian","ru.bicycle","ru.electric_bicycle","ru.electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"'any person' in a crosswalk crossing the street: a person on foot or in a wheelchair (ru.pedestrian 'a person on foot, in a wheelchair, or on a device the jurisdiction treats as on foot'; its exclusion 'a person on a bicycle or scooter' is why the riders are named beside it), or a person riding a bicycle (ru.bicycle), an electric bicycle (ru.electric_bicycle) or an electric scooter (ru.electric_scooter) across it."},{"span":"k9","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.crosswalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"'attempting to cross' is a purpose, read through the conduct it explains: the person's presence in the crosswalk (rel.occupies(o, cw), st.crosswalk), which lies across the street."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), occupies a carrier c (st.travel_region) with st.lane_enters(c, j) for an intersection j; a zone sign of kind school_crossing (dev.zone_sign) governs c (dev.governs); a crosswalk cw (st.crosswalk) marks c's entrance (st.entrance_of(cw, c)); and some road user o, other than the subject, of class ru.pedestrian, ru.bicycle, ru.electric_bicycle or ru.electric_scooter, occupies cw on the subject's side of the roadway: with cl a centre line (st.centre_line) and cw both lying on one way w (st.on_way, st.highway), L = prim.region_lateral_offset(subject, cl) and y the lateral component of rel.bearing(subject, o), L > 0 and y < L, or L < 0 and y > L; or the subject occupies a one-way roadway (st.one_way_roadway).","obligation":"The subject's occupancy of cw does not rise at this observation (rel.occupies(subject, cw) does not hold here while it did not hold at the previous observation), for the cw bound in the applicability, re-bound with the same selection (crosswalk marking the entrance of the carrier c the subject occupies, c governed by the school_crossing sign, a person of the named classes in cw on the subject's side).","params":[],"narrowings":[{"span":"k4","why":"'the operator of any vehicle' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"k5","why":"'displayed' is read through the sign's presence governing the subject's approach carrier; the crosswalk is the one recorded as marking that carrier's entrance","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"k9","why":"'attempting to cross the street' is read through the person's presence in the crosswalk","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A school_crossing sign governs the subject's lane; a child walks in the crosswalk on the subject's half of the roadway; the subject drives into the crosswalk."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same, but the subject halts short of the crosswalk until the child has left it."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"No school_crossing sign governs the subject's lane; a pedestrian is in the crosswalk."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The sign is present but the source does not observe which carriers it governs; the subject drives into an occupied crosswalk.","masked":["dev.governs"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The pedestrian is in the crosswalk on the far side of the centre line when the subject drives in."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_20_060_o1","law_refs":["LVMC-11-20-060"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"The driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"e2","text":"within a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"e3","text":"emerging or entering an alley, driveway or building","role":"condition"},{"id":"e4","text":"shall stop such vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"e5","text":"immediately prior to driving onto a sidewalk or onto the sidewalk area extending across any alleyway or driveway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e6","text":"yielding","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e7","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e8","text":"to any pedestrian","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e9","text":"as may be necessary to avoid collision","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e10","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e11","text":"upon entering the roadway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e12","text":"shall yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e13","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e14","text":"to all vehicles approaching on said roadway","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'The driver of' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency), which ru.aggregate's exclusion of 'who drives or controls a vehicle' requires."},{"span":"e3","atoms":["st.driveway_or_alley_entrance","st.alley","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.driveway_or_alley_entrance 'private road, alley or driveway meeting the highway' and st.alley 'a narrow way within a block serving the rear of properties': the subject emerges from or enters one where its footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies) as it reaches the sidewalk. A building's vehicle access is a driveway: DEF-NRS-484A-190 'every way or place in private ownership and used for vehicular travel'. The exclusion 'which of them meets the highway there' does not matter: the words treat alley, driveway and building alike."},{"span":"e4","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"'stop', required here, is DEF-NRS-484A-255 'complete cessation from movement' (DEF-NRS-484A-260 governs stopping 'when prohibited'), carried by drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance."},{"span":"e5","atoms":["st.sidewalk","rel.occupies","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.sidewalk 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line' (its exclusion 'a crosswalk' does not apply); the sidewalk area across a driveway or alley is the sidewalk region the source maps across the entrance. 'driving onto' is the observation at which rel.occupies(subject, s) rises; 'immediately prior' places the halt outside s within p.stop_point_tolerance of it, the ground distance from the body to s (st.region_geometry 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it')."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[{"span":"e2","id":"asm.business_or_residence_district","meaning":"the place of the road user at the observation lies in a business district or a residence district, as the map's reading classifies the area"}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"asm.business_or_residence_district holds; the subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), begins at this observation to occupy a sidewalk region s (st.sidewalk; rel.occupies(subject, s) here and not at the previous observation) while it occupies a driveway-or-alley-entrance region or an alley region d (st.driveway_or_alley_entrance or st.alley).","obligation":"Event: the entry onto s judged. Place: outside s (rel.occupies(subject, s) false) with the ground distance from the subject's body to s (st.region_geometry) at most p.stop_point_tolerance — the stop zone. Act: drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; p.halt_speed_tolerance) at an observation in the stop zone. Search: back from the observation before the entry through the unbroken run of observations at which the subject was in the stop zone (written as: (in the stop zone, or the entry observation itself) since (in the stop zone and halted)). The run ends at the last observation at which the subject was outside the zone upstream (farther than p.stop_point_tolerance from s and not on it) or on s (the previous entry onto s for the same s); nothing else ends it — not a change of carrier, a reverse within the zone, or speed noise. Met where a halt lies in the run; violated where the run ends at an observed observation outside the zone or on s with no halt; unknown where the run reaches the start of the recording without a halt, or where the speed, occupancy or distance is missing at an observation the verdict turns on. A halt before the previous entry onto s does not count for this entry.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e1","why":"'The driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e5","why":"'immediately prior' is read as a halt within p.stop_point_tolerance of the sidewalk, outside it, in the run of observations the subject spends in that zone before driving onto it","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"District assumed; the subject leaves a driveway and rolls onto the sidewalk at walking pace without its speed ever falling to the halt tolerance in the stop zone, having approached from beyond the zone."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same, but the subject halts within p.stop_point_tolerance of the sidewalk edge before driving onto it."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The trace declares the area outside any business or residence district."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"District assumed; the subject's speed is not observed in the stop zone; it then drives onto the sidewalk.","masked":["kin.speed"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"The subject halts far up the driveway, outside the stop zone, then rolls through the zone onto the sidewalk without halting again."},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The recording begins with the subject already in the stop zone, moving slowly; no halt is recorded before it drives onto the sidewalk, and the run reaches the start of the recording.","boundary":"the approach start: the last observation at which the subject was outside the stop zone upstream, which precedes the recording"}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed noise floor of vehicle odometry and tracked-object estimates"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"the body-to-mark gap within which a halt counts as at the mark: a stop line's set-back before a crossing plus a placement margin","source":"MUTCD 3B.16 (stop line placed 4 ft in advance of a crosswalk) plus driver placement margin"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_20_060_o2","law_refs":["LVMC-11-20-060"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"The driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"e2","text":"within a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"e3","text":"emerging or entering an alley, driveway or building","role":"condition"},{"id":"e4","text":"shall stop such vehicle","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e5","text":"immediately prior to driving onto a sidewalk or onto the sidewalk area extending across any alleyway or driveway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e6","text":"yielding","role":"obligation"},{"id":"e7","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"e8","text":"to any pedestrian","role":"condition"},{"id":"e9","text":"as may be necessary to avoid collision","role":"standard"},{"id":"e10","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e11","text":"upon entering the roadway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e12","text":"shall yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e13","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e14","text":"to all vehicles approaching on said roadway","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'The driver of' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency)."},{"span":"e3","atoms":["st.driveway_or_alley_entrance","st.alley","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"As LVMC_11_20_060_o1: st.driveway_or_alley_entrance 'private road, alley or driveway meeting the highway', st.alley 'a narrow way within a block'; a building's vehicle access is a driveway (DEF-NRS-484A-190 'every way or place in private ownership and used for vehicular travel'); the subject occupies one (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"e5","atoms":["st.sidewalk","rel.occupies","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"The yielding accompanies driving onto the sidewalk: the duty runs while the subject occupies the sidewalk region s (st.sidewalk 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line', rel.occupies) or is in the stop zone before it, its body within p.stop_point_tolerance of s (st.region_geometry ground distance)."},{"span":"e6","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.contact"],"derived":[],"justification":"To yield is not to proceed in preference: kin.speed 'magnitude of velocity' tells a subject still proceeding; rel.contact 'touch or overlap (a collision)' is precedence taken outright; its exclusion 'a near miss' is respected (the near conflict is bounded by the operationalizations)."},{"span":"e8","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrian' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian (ru.aggregate 'membership of a legal aggregate'); 'any' = every member present."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"e7","standard":"right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210 'approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other'","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","kin.speed"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: danger of a crash where the constant-velocity closest approach of centres is below a centre clearance within a time-to-collision horizon","surrogate":false},{"span":"e9","standard":"as may be necessary to avoid collision","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","rel.contact"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: yielding is necessary exactly where a collision would follow under constant velocities, a closest approach below the centre clearance within the horizon","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[{"span":"e2","id":"asm.business_or_residence_district","meaning":"the place of the road user at the observation lies in a business district or a residence district, as the map's reading classifies the area"}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"asm.business_or_residence_district holds; the subject, a vehicle, occupies a driveway-or-alley-entrance region or an alley region d (st.driveway_or_alley_entrance or st.alley), and occupies a sidewalk region s (st.sidewalk) or is within p.stop_point_tolerance of it (st.region_geometry ground distance).","obligation":"For every road user p, other than the subject, that is a pedestrian (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian): not (the subject's kin.speed exceeds p.halt_speed_tolerance while prim.closest_approach_within(subject, p; p.conflict_horizon) holds with prim.closest_approach_distance(subject, p; p.conflict_horizon) below p.conflict_centre_clearance), and not rel.contact(subject, p).","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e1","why":"'The driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e7","why":"precedence is read as the subject not proceeding while a constant-velocity closest approach to the pedestrian falls below the centre clearance within the horizon, and never touching the pedestrian","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"District assumed; the subject crosses the sidewalk out of a driveway while a pedestrian walks toward its path; the closest approach falls below the clearance within the horizon and the subject keeps moving."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same, but the subject waits halted at the sidewalk edge until the pedestrian has passed."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject travels on the roadway, nowhere near a driveway or sidewalk."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"District assumed; the subject crosses the sidewalk with a pedestrian approaching, but the subject's speed is not observed.","masked":["kin.speed"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"District assumed; the subject crosses the sidewalk out of a driveway with no other road user in the scene."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique","source":"Hayward (1972); Hydén (1987)"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies collide or nearly collide","source":"passenger-car dimensions (AASHTO design vehicle P)"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the source's speed resolution","source":"speed noise floor of odometry and tracked-object estimates"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"body-to-mark gap within which a halt counts as at the mark","source":"MUTCD 3B.16 plus placement margin"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_20_060_o3","law_refs":["LVMC-11-20-060"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"The driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"e2","text":"within a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"e3","text":"emerging or entering an alley, driveway or building","role":"condition"},{"id":"e4","text":"shall stop such vehicle","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e5","text":"immediately prior to driving onto a sidewalk or onto the sidewalk area extending across any alleyway or driveway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e6","text":"yielding","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e7","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e8","text":"to any pedestrian","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e9","text":"as may be necessary to avoid collision","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e10","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e11","text":"upon entering the roadway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e12","text":"shall yield","role":"obligation"},{"id":"e13","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"e14","text":"to all vehicles approaching on said roadway","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'The driver of' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency)."},{"span":"e3","atoms":["st.driveway_or_alley_entrance","st.alley","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"As LVMC_11_20_060_o1; for entering the roadway only 'emerging' applies: the subject has occupied the driveway-or-alley-entrance or alley region d (st.driveway_or_alley_entrance 'private road, alley or driveway meeting the highway', st.alley, rel.occupies) continuously since an observation at which it occupied d and not the roadway."},{"span":"e11","atoms":["st.roadway","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.roadway 'the part of a highway improved for vehicular traffic, excluding shoulder' (its exclusion 'the sidewalk' respected); entering it is the subject's footprint overlapping it (rel.occupies) while still on d."},{"span":"e12","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.contact"],"derived":[],"justification":"To yield is not to proceed in preference: kin.speed 'magnitude of velocity'; rel.contact 'touch or overlap (a collision)', whose exclusion 'a near miss' is respected (the near conflict is bounded by the operationalization)."},{"span":"e14","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","rel.occupies","st.roadway","prim.closest_approach_within"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicles' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'on said roadway' is the same roadway r the subject enters (rel.occupies(o, r), st.roadway); 'approaching' is the constant-velocity approach of the centres within the horizon (prim.closest_approach_within 'the centres of two road users approach each other at some time between the observation and the horizon'; its exclusion of contact and danger is respected: danger is the operationalization's bound)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"e13","standard":"right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210 'approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other'","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","kin.speed"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: danger of a crash where the constant-velocity closest approach of centres is below a centre clearance within a time-to-collision horizon; a road user at or below the speed resolution has granted precedence","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[{"span":"e2","id":"asm.business_or_residence_district","meaning":"the place of the road user at the observation lies in a business district or a residence district, as the map's reading classifies the area"}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"asm.business_or_residence_district holds; the subject, a vehicle, occupies a roadway region r (st.roadway) and a driveway-or-alley-entrance or alley region d, having occupied d at every observation since an observation at which it occupied d and not r (it is emerging onto r).","obligation":"For every road user o, other than the subject, that is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and occupies the same r: not (the subject's kin.speed exceeds p.halt_speed_tolerance while prim.closest_approach_within(subject, o; p.conflict_horizon) holds with prim.closest_approach_distance(subject, o; p.conflict_horizon) below p.conflict_centre_clearance), and not rel.contact(subject, o).","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e1","why":"'The driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e13","why":"precedence is read as the subject not proceeding while a constant-velocity closest approach to the approaching vehicle falls below the centre clearance within the horizon, and never touching it","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"District assumed; the subject pulls out of a driveway into the roadway in front of a car approaching on it; the closest approach falls below the clearance within the horizon while the subject keeps moving."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same, but the subject waits at the roadway edge, halted, until the car has passed."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject turns from the roadway into a driveway (it occupied the roadway before the driveway): it is not emerging."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"District assumed; the subject emerges in front of an approaching car, but the source does not supply roadway occupancy.","masked":["rel.occupies"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"District assumed; the subject emerges onto the roadway with no other road user in the scene."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.conflict_horizon","unit":"s","value":3.0,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of the traffic-conflict technique","source":"Hayward (1972); Hydén (1987)"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies collide or nearly collide","source":"passenger-car dimensions (AASHTO design vehicle P)"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the source's speed resolution","source":"speed noise floor of odometry and tracked-object estimates"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_22_010","law_refs":["LVMC-11-22-010"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"h1","text":"A person","role":"subject"},{"id":"h2","text":"shall","role":"obligation"},{"id":"h3","text":"when operating a vehicle","role":"condition"},{"id":"h4","text":"give his full time and attention to the operation of the vehicle","role":"standard"}],"elements":[{"span":"h1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"The person is the one operating the vehicle, read through the vehicle's controlled motion; the vehicle is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, and ru.aggregate's exclusion of 'who drives or controls a vehicle' is respected: the role is read through motion."},{"span":"h2","atoms":["rel.contact"],"derived":[],"justification":"The duty's conduct is checked through its outcome: the vehicle's body does not touch another road user or a structure (rel.contact 'the bodies of two road users, or a road user and a structure, touch or overlap (a collision)'; its exclusion 'a near miss' is respected — the near conflict is the operationalization's bound)."},{"span":"h3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","kin.speed"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'operating' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion: kin.speed 'magnitude of velocity' above p.halt_speed_tolerance."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"h4","standard":"full time and attention to the operation of the vehicle","concepts":["rel.contact","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance"],"params":["p.attention_ttc_min","p.conflict_centre_clearance"],"convention":"surrogate safety measure for inattention: a driver who attends to the driving task neither collides nor closes on the road user ahead in its lane to a time-to-collision below the rear-end conflict threshold","surrogate":true}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), is in motion: its kin.speed exceeds p.halt_speed_tolerance.","obligation":"The subject is in contact (rel.contact) with no road user and no structure; and for every road user o ahead of the subject in its lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane): not (prim.closest_approach_within(subject, o; p.attention_ttc_min) holds with prim.closest_approach_distance(subject, o; p.attention_ttc_min) below p.conflict_centre_clearance).","params":["p.attention_ttc_min","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"h3","why":"'operating' is read through the vehicle's motion; a halted vehicle with its engine running is not judged","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"h4","why":"attention, a state of mind, is read only through its outcome on the road: no collision and no rear-end time-to-collision below the threshold; distraction that shows in no such outcome is not read","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"The subject closes on a halted vehicle ahead in its lane at constant speed; the closest approach falls below the clearance within p.attention_ttc_min."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject follows a vehicle ahead at a steady gap, never closing within the threshold, and touches nothing."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject is halted at a signal."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The subject's speed is not observed.","masked":["kin.speed"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"The subject drives alone on an empty road, touching nothing."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.attention_ttc_min","unit":"s","value":1.5,"convention":"time-to-collision threshold of a critical rear-end conflict","source":"van der Horst (1990) rear-end TTC thresholds"},{"name":"p.conflict_centre_clearance","unit":"m","value":3.0,"convention":"centre-to-centre distance at the closest approach below which the bodies collide or nearly collide","source":"passenger-car dimensions (AASHTO design vehicle P)"},{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the source's speed resolution","source":"speed noise floor of odometry and tracked-object estimates"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"concept_id":"drv.motion.complete_halt","kind":"formula","contract":"The road user is at rest at the observation — \"complete cessation from movement\" — observed as its speed (kin.speed) at or below a tolerance the caller sets for the source's speed resolution. It denotes a state at one observation: it says nothing of how long the road user stays at rest, where it is, or why. Not denoted: a slowing whose sampled speed stays above the tolerance.","definition":"DEF-NRS-484A-255","args":[{"name":"a","sort":"track"}],"params":[{"name":"speed_tol","unit":"m/s","meaning":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution"}],"elements":[{"span":"its speed (kin.speed) at or below a tolerance","atoms":["kin.speed"],"concepts":[],"justification":"kin.speed 'magnitude of velocity' in m/s; an absolute cessation is observed over sampled speeds only within the caller's tolerance. Its exclusion of acceleration does not apply."}],"residues":[{"span":"when required","why":"the scope of the definition (a stop that a law requires) is decided by the law that calls the concept, not by the state observed"}],"literals":[],"scenarios":[{"name":"holds","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A vehicle's sampled speed is at the tolerance or below."},{"name":"fails","expected":"violated","narrative":"A vehicle creeps forward with a sampled speed above the tolerance."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The source does not observe the road user's speed.","masked":["kin.speed"]}],"used_by":["LVMC_11_20_060_o1"],"supersedes":null}

