{"node_id":"LVMC_11_18_020","law_refs":["LVMC-11-18-020"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"k1","text":"The City Traffic Engineer is authorized to mark and maintain with yellow paint or road buttons crosswalks approximately twelve feet in width at intersections in the vicinity of schools where in the opinion of the City Traffic Engineer crossing the roadway by schoolchildren is unsafe.","role":"definitional"},{"id":"k2","text":"The City Traffic Engineer, if necessary, is further authorized to mark and maintain with a distinguishing color or road buttons upon the pavement or by signs erected along the curb in a conspicuous manner, the words \"School-Xing,\" not less than one hundred feet in advance of each crosswalk established","role":"definitional"},{"id":"k3","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"k4","text":"it shall be unlawful for the operator of any vehicle to drive into a crosswalk","role":"obligation"},{"id":"k5","text":"where there is displayed a sign with the words \"School-Xing,\"","role":"condition"},{"id":"k6","text":"when there is in the crosswalk","role":"condition"},{"id":"k7","text":"upon the side of the roadway on which said vehicle is coming","role":"condition"},{"id":"k8","text":"any person","role":"condition"},{"id":"k9","text":"attempting to cross the street","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"k4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","rel.occupies","st.crosswalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'the operator of' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency), never as membership. 'drive into a crosswalk' is the observation at which the subject's footprint begins to overlap (rel.occupies rises) a crosswalk cw (st.crosswalk 'marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection'); 'Not a stand-in for' clauses of rel.occupies are none, and st.sidewalk's exclusion of crosswalks is not engaged."},{"span":"k5","atoms":["dev.zone_sign","dev.governs","st.entrance_of","st.lane_enters","rel.occupies","st.travel_region","st.intersection","st.crosswalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"dev.zone_sign 'a sign that begins or ends a signed zone along the road; kind ∈ {school, school_crossing, ...}': the 'School-Xing' sign is kind school_crossing. It is the sign of that crosswalk: it governs (dev.governs 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls') the carrier c the subject occupies (rel.occupies), whose entrance into intersection j (st.lane_enters) the crosswalk marks (st.entrance_of 'the carrier whose entrance into an intersection a stop line or a crosswalk marks'). dev.zone_sign's exclusion 'whether the condition holds now' is respected: no condition of the legend is read; dev.governs 'Not a stand-in for: a position' does not apply."},{"span":"k6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.crosswalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"The person o is in the crosswalk cw the subject drives into: rel.occupies(o, cw) 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region (... crosswalk ...)'."},{"span":"k7","atoms":["st.centre_line","prim.region_lateral_offset","rel.bearing","st.on_way","st.highway","st.one_way_roadway"],"derived":[],"justification":"The side of the roadway the subject comes on is its side of the centre line (st.centre_line 'the marking, or the geometric centre, dividing the two directions of a two-way roadway') of the way w the crosswalk lies on (st.on_way(cw, w), st.on_way(cl, w), st.highway). With L = prim.region_lateral_offset(subject, cl) ('the signed lateral offset ... of a structure region from a road user', left positive) and y the lateral component of rel.bearing(subject, o) ('direction of b from a in a's frame'), o is on the subject's side where L > 0 and y < L, or L < 0 and y > L. Where the subject occupies a one-way roadway (st.one_way_roadway 'roadway on which traffic is restricted to one direction'), the whole crosswalk is its side."},{"span":"k8","atoms":["ru.pedestrian","ru.bicycle","ru.electric_bicycle","ru.electric_scooter"],"derived":[],"justification":"'any person' in a crosswalk crossing the street: a person on foot or in a wheelchair (ru.pedestrian 'a person on foot, in a wheelchair, or on a device the jurisdiction treats as on foot'; its exclusion 'a person on a bicycle or scooter' is why the riders are named beside it), or a person riding a bicycle (ru.bicycle), an electric bicycle (ru.electric_bicycle) or an electric scooter (ru.electric_scooter) across it."},{"span":"k9","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.crosswalk"],"derived":[],"justification":"'attempting to cross' is a purpose, read through the conduct it explains: the person's presence in the crosswalk (rel.occupies(o, cw), st.crosswalk), which lies across the street."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), occupies a carrier c (st.travel_region) with st.lane_enters(c, j) for an intersection j; a zone sign of kind school_crossing (dev.zone_sign) governs c (dev.governs); a crosswalk cw (st.crosswalk) marks c's entrance (st.entrance_of(cw, c)); and some road user o, other than the subject, of class ru.pedestrian, ru.bicycle, ru.electric_bicycle or ru.electric_scooter, occupies cw on the subject's side of the roadway: with cl a centre line (st.centre_line) and cw both lying on one way w (st.on_way, st.highway), L = prim.region_lateral_offset(subject, cl) and y the lateral component of rel.bearing(subject, o), L > 0 and y < L, or L < 0 and y > L; or the subject occupies a one-way roadway (st.one_way_roadway).","obligation":"The subject's occupancy of cw does not rise at this observation (rel.occupies(subject, cw) does not hold here while it did not hold at the previous observation), for the cw bound in the applicability, re-bound with the same selection (crosswalk marking the entrance of the carrier c the subject occupies, c governed by the school_crossing sign, a person of the named classes in cw on the subject's side).","params":[],"narrowings":[{"span":"k4","why":"'the operator of any vehicle' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"k5","why":"'displayed' is read through the sign's presence governing the subject's approach carrier; the crosswalk is the one recorded as marking that carrier's entrance","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"k9","why":"'attempting to cross the street' is read through the person's presence in the crosswalk","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A school_crossing sign governs the subject's lane; a child walks in the crosswalk on the subject's half of the roadway; the subject drives into the crosswalk."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same, but the subject halts short of the crosswalk until the child has left it."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"No school_crossing sign governs the subject's lane; a pedestrian is in the crosswalk."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The sign is present but the source does not observe which carriers it governs; the subject drives into an occupied crosswalk.","masked":["dev.governs"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The pedestrian is in the crosswalk on the far side of the centre line when the subject drives in."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_20_060_o1","law_refs":["LVMC-11-20-060"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"The driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"e2","text":"within a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"e3","text":"emerging or entering an alley, driveway or building","role":"condition"},{"id":"e4","text":"shall stop such vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"e5","text":"immediately prior to driving onto a sidewalk or onto the sidewalk area extending across any alleyway or driveway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e6","text":"yielding","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e7","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e8","text":"to any pedestrian","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e9","text":"as may be necessary to avoid collision","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e10","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e11","text":"upon entering the roadway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e12","text":"shall yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e13","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e14","text":"to all vehicles approaching on said roadway","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'The driver of' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency), which ru.aggregate's exclusion of 'who drives or controls a vehicle' requires."},{"span":"e3","atoms":["st.driveway_or_alley_entrance","st.alley","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.driveway_or_alley_entrance 'private road, alley or driveway meeting the highway' and st.alley 'a narrow way within a block serving the rear of properties': the subject emerges from or enters one where its footprint overlaps it (rel.occupies) as it reaches the sidewalk. A building's vehicle access is a driveway: DEF-NRS-484A-190 'every way or place in private ownership and used for vehicular travel'. The exclusion 'which of them meets the highway there' does not matter: the words treat alley, driveway and building alike."},{"span":"e4","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"'stop', required here, is DEF-NRS-484A-255 'complete cessation from movement' (DEF-NRS-484A-260 governs stopping 'when prohibited'), carried by drv.motion.complete_halt with p.halt_speed_tolerance."},{"span":"e5","atoms":["st.sidewalk","rel.occupies","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"st.sidewalk 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line' (its exclusion 'a crosswalk' does not apply); the sidewalk area across a driveway or alley is the sidewalk region the source maps across the entrance. 'driving onto' is the observation at which rel.occupies(subject, s) rises; 'immediately prior' places the halt outside s within p.stop_point_tolerance of it, the ground distance from the body to s (st.region_geometry 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it')."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[{"span":"e2","id":"asm.business_or_residence_district","meaning":"the place of the road user at the observation lies in a business district or a residence district, as the map's reading classifies the area"}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"asm.business_or_residence_district holds; the subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), begins at this observation to occupy a sidewalk region s (st.sidewalk; rel.occupies(subject, s) here and not at the previous observation) while it occupies a driveway-or-alley-entrance region or an alley region d (st.driveway_or_alley_entrance or st.alley).","obligation":"Event: the entry onto s judged. Place: outside s (rel.occupies(subject, s) false) with the ground distance from the subject's body to s (st.region_geometry) at most p.stop_point_tolerance — the stop zone. Act: drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; p.halt_speed_tolerance) at an observation in the stop zone. Search: back from the observation before the entry through the unbroken run of observations at which the subject was in the stop zone (written as: (in the stop zone, or the entry observation itself) since (in the stop zone and halted)). The run ends at the last observation at which the subject was outside the zone upstream (farther than p.stop_point_tolerance from s and not on it) or on s (the previous entry onto s for the same s); nothing else ends it — not a change of carrier, a reverse within the zone, or speed noise. Met where a halt lies in the run; violated where the run ends at an observed observation outside the zone or on s with no halt; unknown where the run reaches the start of the recording without a halt, or where the speed, occupancy or distance is missing at an observation the verdict turns on. A halt before the previous entry onto s does not count for this entry.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e1","why":"'The driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e5","why":"'immediately prior' is read as a halt within p.stop_point_tolerance of the sidewalk, outside it, in the run of observations the subject spends in that zone before driving onto it","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"District assumed; the subject leaves a driveway and rolls onto the sidewalk at walking pace without its speed ever falling to the halt tolerance in the stop zone, having approached from beyond the zone."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same, but the subject halts within p.stop_point_tolerance of the sidewalk edge before driving onto it."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The trace declares the area outside any business or residence district."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"District assumed; the subject's speed is not observed in the stop zone; it then drives onto the sidewalk.","masked":["kin.speed"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"The subject halts far up the driveway, outside the stop zone, then rolls through the zone onto the sidewalk without halting again."},{"name":"history_boundary","expected":"unknown","narrative":"The recording begins with the subject already in the stop zone, moving slowly; no halt is recorded before it drives onto the sidewalk, and the run reaches the start of the recording.","boundary":"the approach start: the last observation at which the subject was outside the stop zone upstream, which precedes the recording"}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed noise floor of vehicle odometry and tracked-object estimates"},{"name":"p.stop_point_tolerance","unit":"m","value":2.0,"convention":"the body-to-mark gap within which a halt counts as at the mark: a stop line's set-back before a crossing plus a placement margin","source":"MUTCD 3B.16 (stop line placed 4 ft in advance of a crosswalk) plus driver placement margin"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_20_060_o2","law_refs":["LVMC-11-20-060"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"e1","text":"The driver of a vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"e2","text":"within a business or residence district","role":"condition"},{"id":"e3","text":"emerging or entering an alley, driveway or building","role":"condition"},{"id":"e4","text":"shall stop such vehicle","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e5","text":"immediately prior to driving onto a sidewalk or onto the sidewalk area extending across any alleyway or driveway","role":"trigger"},{"id":"e6","text":"yielding","role":"obligation"},{"id":"e7","text":"the right-of-way","role":"standard"},{"id":"e8","text":"to any pedestrian","role":"condition"},{"id":"e9","text":"as may be necessary to avoid collision","role":"standard"},{"id":"e10","text":"and","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e11","text":"upon entering the roadway","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e12","text":"shall yield","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e13","text":"the right-of-way","role":"sibling"},{"id":"e14","text":"to all vehicles approaching on said roadway","role":"sibling"}],"elements":[{"span":"e1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'The driver of' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (agency)."},{"span":"e3","atoms":["st.driveway_or_alley_entrance","st.alley","rel.occupies"],"derived":[],"justification":"As LVMC_11_20_060_o1: st.driveway_or_alley_entrance 'private road, alley or driveway meeting the highway', st.alley 'a narrow way within a block'; a building's vehicle access is a driveway (DEF-NRS-484A-190 'every way or place in private ownership and used for vehicular travel'); the subject occupies one (rel.occupies)."},{"span":"e5","atoms":["st.sidewalk","rel.occupies","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"The yielding accompanies driving onto the sidewalk: the duty runs while the subject occupies the sidewalk region s (st.sidewalk 'area for pedestrians between roadway and property line', rel.occupies) or is in the stop zone before it, its body within p.stop_point_tolerance of s (st.region_geometry ground distance)."},{"span":"e6","atoms":["kin.speed","rel.contact"],"derived":[],"justification":"To yield is not to proceed in preference: kin.speed 'magnitude of velocity' tells a subject still proceeding; rel.contact 'touch or overlap (a collision)' is precedence taken outright; its exclusion 'a near miss' is respected (the near conflict is bounded by the operationalizations)."},{"span":"e8","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian"],"derived":[],"justification":"'pedestrian' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian (ru.aggregate 'membership of a legal aggregate'); 'any' = every member present."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"e7","standard":"right-of-way: DEF-NRS-484A-210 'approaching under such circumstances of direction, speed and proximity as to give rise to the danger of a crash unless one grants precedence to the other'","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","kin.speed"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: danger of a crash where the constant-velocity closest approach of centres is below a centre clearance within a time-to-collision horizon","surrogate":false},{"span":"e9","standard":"as may be necessary to avoid collision","concepts":["prim.closest_approach_within","prim.closest_approach_distance","rel.contact"],"params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance"],"convention":"traffic-conflict technique: yielding is necessary exactly where a collision would follow under constant velocities, a closest approach below the centre clearance within the horizon","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[{"span":"e2","id":"asm.business_or_residence_district","meaning":"the place of the road user at the observation lies in a business district or a residence district, as the map's reading classifies the area"}],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"asm.business_or_residence_district holds; the subject, a vehicle, occupies a driveway-or-alley-entrance region or an alley region d (st.driveway_or_alley_entrance or st.alley), and occupies a sidewalk region s (st.sidewalk) or is within p.stop_point_tolerance of it (st.region_geometry ground distance).","obligation":"For every road user p, other than the subject, that is a pedestrian (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian): not (the subject's kin.speed exceeds p.halt_speed_tolerance while prim.closest_approach_within(subject, p; p.conflict_horizon) holds with prim.closest_approach_distance(subject, p; p.conflict_horizon) below p.conflict_centre_clearance), and not rel.contact(subject, p).","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.stop_point_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e1","why":"'The driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e7","why":"precedence is read as the subject not proceeding while a constant-velocity closest approach to the pedestrian falls below the centre clearance within the horizon, and never touching the pedestrian","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"District assumed; the subject crosses the sidewalk out of a driveway while a pedestrian walks toward its path; the closest approach falls below the clearance within the horizon and the subject keeps moving."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same, but the subject waits halted at the sidewalk edge until the pedestrian has passed."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject travels on the ro