[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"asm.business_or_residence_district holds; the subject, a vehicle, occupies a roadway region r (st.roadway) and a driveway-or-alley-entrance or alley region d, having occupied d at every observation since an observation at which it occupied d and not r (it is emerging onto r).","obligation":"For every road user o, other than the subject, that is a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and occupies the same r: not (the subject's kin.speed exceeds p.halt_speed_tolerance while prim.closest_approach_within(subject, o; p.conflict_horizon) holds with prim.closest_approach_distance(subject, o; p.conflict_horizon) below p.conflict_centre_clearance), and not rel.contact(subject, o).","params":["p.conflict_horizon","p.conflict_centre_clearance","p.halt_speed_tolerance"],"narrowings":[{"span":"e1","why":"'The driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion","kind":"observable_reading","category":"agency"},{"span":"e13","why":"precedence is read as the subject not proceeding while a constant-velocity closest approach to the approaching vehicle falls below the centre clearance within the horizon, and never touching it","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"District assumed; the subject pulls out of a driveway into the roadway in front of a car approaching on it; the closest approach falls below the clearance within the horizon while the subject keeps moving."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"Same, but the subject waits at the roadway edge, halted, until the car has passed."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"The subject turns from the roadway into a driveway (it occupied the roadway before the driveway): it is not emerging."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"District assumed; the subject emerges in front of an approa